{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "iacms-auth-collection",
    "name": "IACMS Authentication",
    "description": "Complete authentication testing collection for IACMS.\n\nIncludes:\n- Health Check\n- JWT Authentication (for API clients)\n- Session Authentication (for web browsers)\n- Admin: Create User (with email + temp password)\n- Password Management (forgot / reset / change)\n- Error Cases\n\n**Test Order:**\n1. Health Check\n2. JWT Login → use {{accessToken}} in all protected requests\n3. Admin creates user → check Mailtrap inbox for temp password\n4. Forgot Password → check Mailtrap inbox → Reset Password\n5. Change Password (logged-in user)",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Auto-set by JWT Login request"
    },
    {
      "key": "refreshToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Auto-set by JWT Login request"
    },
    {
      "key": "resetToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Manually paste the token from the Mailtrap reset email URL"
    },
    {
      "key": "createdUserId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Auto-set when admin creates a user"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Health & Setup",
      "description": "Verify services are running before testing",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "API Gateway Health",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Gateway is healthy', function () {",
                  "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.status).to.equal('ok');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Session auth enabled', function () {",
                  "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.features.sessionAuth).to.be.true;",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["health"]
            },
            "description": "Check if API Gateway is running.\n\n**Expected:**\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"features\": {\n    \"sessionAuth\": true,\n    \"jwtAuth\": true\n  }\n}\n```"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Auth Service Health (Direct)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://localhost:3001/health",
              "host": ["http://localhost:3001"],
              "path": ["health"]
            },
            "description": "Check if Auth Service is running directly on port 3001."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. JWT Authentication (API Clients)",
      "description": "Token-based authentication for mobile apps and API clients.\n\n**Flow:**\n1. Login → get accessToken + refreshToken\n2. Send `Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}` on protected requests\n3. Use Refresh Token when access token expires",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "JWT Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "if (jsonData.accessToken) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', jsonData.accessToken);",
                  "    console.log('✓ Access token saved');",
                  "}",
                  "if (jsonData.refreshToken) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', jsonData.refreshToken);",
                  "    console.log('✓ Refresh token saved');",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Has accessToken', () => pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('accessToken'));",
                  "pm.test('Has refreshToken', () => pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('refreshToken'));",
                  "pm.test('Has user data', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.user).to.have.property('email');",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.user).to.have.property('id');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"admin@test-org.com\",\n  \"password\": \"password123\",\n  \"tenantCode\": \"TEST-ORG\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Login with email + password to receive JWT tokens.\n\nTokens are **auto-saved** to collection variables `{{accessToken}}` and `{{refreshToken}}`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Profile (JWT)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Has user data', () => {",
                  "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.user).to.have.property('email');",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.user).to.have.property('mustChangePassword');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}"}],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/profile",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "profile"]
            },
            "description": "Get current user's profile using JWT Bearer token.\n\nResponse now includes `mustChangePassword` flag — if `true`, the user was created by an admin and must change their password."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh Token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (jsonData.accessToken) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', jsonData.accessToken);",
                  "    console.log('✓ New access token saved');",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Has new accessToken', () => pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('accessToken'));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/refresh",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "refresh"]
            },
            "description": "Get a new access token using the refresh token.\nCall this when the access token has expired (after 24h)."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Session Authentication (Web Browsers)",
      "description": "Cookie-based authentication for web browsers.\n\n**Flow:**\n1. Session Login → `iacms.sid` cookie set automatically\n2. Subsequent requests use the cookie (no header needed)\n3. Session Logout → cookie cleared",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Session Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Auth method is session', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().authMethod).to.equal('session');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Cookie was set', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.cookies.has('iacms.sid')).to.be.true;",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"admin@test-org.com\",\n  \"password\": \"password123\",\n  \"tenantCode\": \"TEST-ORG\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/session/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "session", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Log in and create a PostgreSQL-backed session.\n\nCheck the **Cookies** tab — you should see `iacms.sid` was set automatically."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Session Status",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('User is authenticated', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().authenticated).to.be.true;",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/session/status",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "session", "status"]
            },
            "description": "Check current session — no Authorization header needed, cookie is sent automatically."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Session Refresh",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/session/refresh",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "session", "refresh"]
            },
            "description": "Extend session expiry time. Useful for keep-alive pings."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Session Logout",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Logout successful', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.equal('Logged out successfully');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/session/logout",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "session", "logout"]
            },
            "description": "Destroy session. Deletes it from PostgreSQL and clears the cookie."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Admin: Create User",
      "description": "Admin-only flow for creating user accounts.\n\n**What happens:**\n1. Admin sends user details (no password needed)\n2. Server generates a secure 12-character temporary password\n3. User is created with `mustChangePassword: true`\n4. Welcome email sent via Mailtrap with login credentials\n\n**Check Mailtrap:** https://mailtrap.io/inboxes\n\n**Requires:** JWT Login first to get `{{accessToken}}`",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create User (Admin)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "if (jsonData.user && jsonData.user.id) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('createdUserId', jsonData.user.id);",
                  "    console.log('✓ Created user ID saved:', jsonData.user.id);",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Status 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('User created with mustChangePassword=true', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.user.mustChangePassword).to.be.true;",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Success message mentions email', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.message).to.include('email');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"},
              {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}"}
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"jane.smith@test-org.com\",\n  \"firstName\": \"Jane\",\n  \"lastName\": \"Smith\",\n  \"username\": \"jane.smith\",\n  \"tenantCode\": \"TEST-ORG\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/users/create",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "users", "create"]
            },
            "description": "Admin creates a new user account.\n\n**No password in the request!** The server generates a secure temporary password automatically.\n\n**After sending:**\n1. Check [Mailtrap](https://mailtrap.io/inboxes) for the welcome email\n2. The email contains the user's temporary password\n3. The user must change it on first login\n\n**Change the email** for each test run — duplicates will return 400."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Create User - Duplicate Email (Should Fail)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 400 Validation Error', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('Error mentions email already exists', () => {",
                  "    var msg = pm.response.json().error.message.toLowerCase();",
                  "    pm.expect(msg).to.include('already exists');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"},
              {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}"}
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"jane.smith@test-org.com\",\n  \"firstName\": \"Jane\",\n  \"lastName\": \"Smith\",\n  \"tenantCode\": \"TEST-ORG\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/users/create",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "users", "create"]
            },
            "description": "Run this **after** Create User succeeds to verify duplicate email is rejected."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Create User - No Auth (Should Fail)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"hacker@test-org.com\",\n  \"firstName\": \"Test\",\n  \"lastName\": \"User\",\n  \"tenantCode\": \"TEST-ORG\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/users/create",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "users", "create"]
            },
            "description": "Try to create a user without an auth token.\n\n**Expected:** 401 Unauthorized"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Password Management",
      "description": "Forgot password and change password flows.\n\n**Forgot Password Flow:**\n1. Send `Forgot Password` request\n2. Open [Mailtrap](https://mailtrap.io/inboxes)\n3. Copy the token from the reset link URL (the `?token=...` part)\n4. Paste into `{{resetToken}}` collection variable\n5. Send `Reset Password` request\n\n**Change Password Flow (logged-in user):**\n1. Ensure you have a valid `{{accessToken}}`\n2. Send `Change Password` with currentPassword + newPassword",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Forgot Password",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Generic success message (no email enumeration)', () => {",
                  "    var msg = pm.response.json().message;",
                  "    pm.expect(msg).to.include('If an account');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "console.log('📧 Check Mailtrap for the reset email: https://mailtrap.io/inboxes');",
                  "console.log('📋 Copy the token from the reset link and paste into {{resetToken}} variable');"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"admin@test-org.com\",\n  \"tenantCode\": \"TEST-ORG\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/forgot-password",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "forgot-password"]
            },
            "description": "Request a password reset link.\n\n**No auth required** — this is a public endpoint.\n\n**After sending:**\n1. Go to [Mailtrap](https://mailtrap.io/inboxes)\n2. Open the reset email\n3. Find the reset link, it looks like: `http://localhost:5173/reset-password?token=abc123...&tenant=TEST-ORG`\n4. Copy the token value (the long string after `?token=`)\n5. Set it as `{{resetToken}}` in collection variables\n6. Then send the `Reset Password` request\n\n**Security note:** Always returns the same message even for unknown emails — prevents email enumeration attacks."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Reset Password",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Password reset successful', () => {",
                  "    var msg = pm.response.json().message;",
                  "    pm.expect(msg).to.include('reset successfully');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Clear the used token",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('resetToken', '');",
                  "console.log('✓ Token cleared. You can now log in with the new password.');"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"token\": \"{{resetToken}}\",\n  \"newPassword\": \"NewPassword123!\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/reset-password",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "reset-password"]
            },
            "description": "Submit the reset token (from email) and set a new password.\n\n**Before sending:**\n1. Complete the `Forgot Password` request\n2. Copy the token from Mailtrap email URL\n3. Paste it into `{{resetToken}}` collection variable\n\n**Token rules:**\n- Expires after **1 hour**\n- Can only be used **once**\n- Single-use: once reset succeeds, token is cleared from DB\n\n**Password requirements:**\n- At least 8 characters\n- At least 1 letter and 1 number"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Reset Password - Expired/Invalid Token (Should Fail)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('Error mentions invalid or expired token', () => {",
                  "    var msg = pm.response.json().error.message.toLowerCase();",
                  "    pm.expect(msg).to.include('invalid or expired');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"token\": \"thisisafaketoken123456789\",\n  \"newPassword\": \"NewPassword123!\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/reset-password",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "reset-password"]
            },
            "description": "Test reset with a fake/expired token.\n\n**Expected:** 400 with 'Invalid or expired' message"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Change Password (Logged-In User)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Password changed', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.include('changed successfully');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "console.log('📧 Check Mailtrap for the password changed confirmation email.');"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"},
              {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}"}
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"currentPassword\": \"password123\",\n  \"newPassword\": \"NewPassword456!\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/change-password",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "change-password"]
            },
            "description": "Logged-in user changes their own password.\n\n**Requires:** Valid `{{accessToken}}` (run JWT Login first)\n\n**Validates:**\n- `currentPassword` must match the account's current password\n- `newPassword` must be different from `currentPassword`\n- `newPassword` must meet strength requirements\n\n**After success:**\n- `mustChangePassword` flag is cleared\n- Confirmation email sent via Mailtrap\n- Check Mailtrap inbox for the confirmation"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Change Password - Wrong Current Password (Should Fail)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('Error mentions incorrect password', () => {",
                  "    var msg = pm.response.json().error.message.toLowerCase();",
                  "    pm.expect(msg).to.include('incorrect');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"},
              {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}"}
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"currentPassword\": \"thisiswrong\",\n  \"newPassword\": \"NewPassword789!\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/change-password",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "change-password"]
            },
            "description": "Try to change password with the wrong current password.\n\n**Expected:** 400 with 'Current password is incorrect'"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "6. Self-Registration",
      "description": "Direct user self-registration (user provides their own password).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register New User",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('Has user and tokens', () => {",
                  "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('user');",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('accessToken');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
